00:22:45.760 --> 00:22:49.679
introduced by [music] a group known as

00:22:47.120 --> 00:22:51.840
the Bogleheads. It sounds complicated,

00:22:49.679 --> 00:22:53.440
but it's actually really simple. You

00:22:51.840 --> 00:22:55.520
could probably hand this setup to a

00:22:53.440 --> 00:22:57.440
total beginner and not only would they

00:22:55.520 --> 00:22:59.600
be able to do it, they'd probably

00:22:57.440 --> 00:23:01.520
outperform a fancy fund manager in a

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:03.840
suit that charges a fortune to manage

00:23:01.520 --> 00:23:06.240
your portfolio. The idea is to invest in

00:23:03.840 --> 00:23:08.400
a domestic fund to capture potential

00:23:06.240 --> 00:23:11.200
returns from your home economy, an

00:23:08.400 --> 00:23:13.600
international fund to diversify across

00:23:11.200 --> 00:23:16.640
other countries, and a bond market fund

00:23:13.600 --> 00:23:18.400
to add some stability. Now, once you

00:23:16.640 --> 00:23:20.559
have this strategy in place, the

00:23:18.400 --> 00:23:23.280
question becomes, how much money do you

00:23:20.559 --> 00:23:25.360
