00:23:23.280 --> 00:23:26.960
completely depends on your age and risk

00:23:25.360 --> 00:23:29.200
tolerance. If you're on the younger

00:23:26.960 --> 00:23:31.600
side, prepared to take more risk and

00:23:29.200 --> 00:23:34.480
want to grow your wealth over time, you

00:23:31.600 --> 00:23:37.039
might go for a 70% domestic, 20%

00:23:34.480 --> 00:23:38.640
international, and 10% bond split.

00:23:37.039 --> 00:23:40.640
Whereas, if you're old and great like

00:23:38.640 --> 00:23:42.559
me, you might be more interested in

00:23:40.640 --> 00:23:45.360
keeping what you have instead of chasing

00:23:42.559 --> 00:23:48.880
returns. So, you might go for 45%

00:23:45.360 --> 00:23:51.919
domestic, 15% international, and 40%

00:23:48.880 --> 00:23:54.559
bonds. As I've said before, I'm not on

00:23:51.919 --> 00:23:56.640
the old man investing style yet, and I

00:23:54.559 --> 00:23:58.880
do lean more towards a younger person

00:23:56.640 --> 00:24:00.960
strategy, but I've been doing this for a

00:23:58.880 --> 00:24:04.000
long time and feel pretty comfortable

00:24:00.960 --> 00:24:06.400
when taking risk. But hey, maybe one day

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:08.880
that'll change. So, let's start with

00:24:06.400 --> 00:24:11.200
