00:45:16.400 --> 00:45:20.480
for thousands of years. Because there's

00:45:18.319 --> 00:45:22.560
a limited supply and it isn't tied to

00:45:20.480 --> 00:45:24.720
the success of any particular company or

00:45:22.560 --> 00:45:26.000
government, investors often turn to it

00:45:24.720 --> 00:45:28.560
when they become worried about

00:45:26.000 --> 00:45:30.960
inflation, financial instability, or

00:45:28.560 --> 00:45:34.160
geopolitical problems. Think of gold

00:45:30.960 --> 00:45:36.240
like a chaos insurance. When people are

00:45:34.160 --> 00:45:38.079
scared and don't know what to trust,

00:45:36.240 --> 00:45:40.480
gold can become attractive because it

00:45:38.079 --> 00:45:42.560
has no earnings to collapse, no CEO to

00:45:40.480 --> 00:45:44.880
mess things up, and no balance sheet to

00:45:42.560 --> 00:45:46.560
go bankrupt. But it's important to

00:45:44.880 --> 00:45:48.960
remember that gold doesn't actually

00:45:46.560 --> 00:45:51.040
produce anything. A bar of gold just

00:45:48.960 --> 00:45:53.119
sits in a vault looking pretty. It

00:45:51.040 --> 00:45:55.280
doesn't ship a product or generate any

00:45:53.119 --> 00:45:57.520
revenue. A great business can take the

00:45:55.280 --> 00:45:59.440
money it earns, reinvest it, and grow

00:45:57.520 --> 00:46:01.839
the profits to potentially become far

00:45:59.440 --> 00:46:03.680
more valuable over time, whereas gold

00:46:01.839 --> 00:46:06.000
can't do that. For you to make money

00:46:03.680 --> 00:46:07.760
from gold, someone else generally has to

00:46:06.000 --> 00:46:10.079
be willing to pay more for it than you

00:46:07.760 --> 00:46:11.760
did. That doesn't make gold bad. In

00:46:10.079 --> 00:46:13.599
fact, it just means it serves a

00:46:11.760 --> 00:46:15.599
different purpose. I recently went to

00:46:13.599 --> 00:46:17.680
Costco and bought a physical bar of gold

00:46:15.599 --> 00:46:20.000
and a gold Bratannia. But doing this

00:46:17.680 --> 00:46:22.079
does have some obvious downsides like

00:46:20.000 --> 00:46:24.000
having to store it somewhere safely, the

00:46:22.079 --> 00:46:25.520
risk of losing it, and having to find

00:46:24.000 --> 00:46:27.920
somewhere to buy it should you want to

00:46:25.520 --> 00:46:29.839
sell. It's much easier to just head over

00:46:27.920 --> 00:46:32.720
to your investing app, which I'll show

00:46:29.839 --> 00:46:35.280
you now. Let's search for gold. And as

00:46:32.720 --> 00:46:38.319
you can see, there's this gold ETF here

00:46:35.280 --> 00:46:40.000
with the ticker GLD. When you invest in

00:46:38.319 --> 00:46:42.000
this, you own a share in a trust that

00:46:40.000 --> 00:46:44.240
holds physical gold. but you don't

00:46:42.000 --> 00:46:46.480
actually hold any yourself, so you can't

00:46:44.240 --> 00:46:48.480
